Subject: Permit normal-coordinate tile-size changes on v2 resume

Review-only proposal. This patch text is not applied to runtime code.

Assessment
==========

`normal_tile_size` in `StreamedPrimitiveNormalFunctional` only partitions the same primitive-coordinate integrals into x tiles. It changes peak temporary memory and the order of floating-point accumulation, but not the basis, quadrature, interaction, density, or mathematical functional. Allowing 8 -> 16/32 is therefore a numerical execution change, not a physics/model change. It can cause small roundoff differences in energy/gradients and thus later Adam/backtracking trajectories; the resume must retain optimizer moments but record that this continuation changed tiling. It must not be described as bitwise-identical continuation.

For this narrowly requested change, keep `normal_chunk_size`, `residual_chunk_size`, `pairing_chunk_size`, and `pairing_active_chunk_size` exact-match. They are also execution partitions in principle, but changing several at once expands the numerical-equivalence claim and makes it harder to attribute any observed differences. Revisit those separately with equivalent partition tests. Keep all physical/model/optimizer compatibility guards strict, including PKA1 and D1S parameters, functional/evaluator identity, PH `lmax`, complete basis metadata (radius, spacing, angular grid, derivative order, kappa/primitive dimension), number targets, model architecture and reference fingerprint, device, number/objective prescription and weights, chemical-potential training, learning rate, AL settings, and trial/backtracking options. `updates_requested` and the fresh-run-only chemical-potential initializer remain continuation exceptions as they are today.

